{"kind":"request","text":"New public demo Worker, dap-demo (part 1: CLI and MCP access).\n\nDecision, 23 October: artroom-scope is no longer the public creation point. Since the 06:42 security deploy (8c344ef1), creation admission on artroom-scope accepts only the register@17 and register@5 cohorts and only its configured register as a parentless install. Its public demo register sc_ncinb5dyvrhtzpos52pbzr2uib3vk5fovqc5nqypfjdxs6kugsmq is pinned to platform:register@8, so new demo rooms there are refused. artroom-scope stays in register mode, so its existing rooms keep answering when someone opens them.\n\nWork, in one head on main:\n1. A reviewed configuration for a new Worker named dap-demo (for example apps/room/wrangler.demo.jsonc). It has its own scope, index, registry and agent namespaces, its own Artifacts namespace, SCOPE_INDEX_MODE enforce, the same serving limits as dap-grow, and no open-creation setting. DEPLOYMENT and SESSION_SECRET are secrets that the planner sets. ARTIFACTS_CONFIG.registerScope comes from the planner's install plan.\n2. An option on dap install (plan, planned and direct forms) that founds a register with policy open instead of keys. The default stays keys. The register uses the archive-device-application cohort (register@17, directory@16, membership@8, rules@10, destination@12, inbox@1), so every room under it passes creation admission.\n3. Docs: docs/cli.md and docs/scopes.md name dap-demo.inguz.workers.dev as the hosted service for new rooms, and say that artroom-scope keeps existing rooms only.\n4. On artroom-scope, the start page says that it makes no new rooms and links to the new address. Use the smallest change: a page notice, or the removal of DEMO_START_CONFIG, with the steps for the planner.\n5. A runbook section: plan the register, deploy with the planned registerScope, set the secrets, install the planned register, create one room as a visitor key, and check that an unlisted scope answers not-found.\n\nWitnesses: an open register admits a room founded by a key outside its founders; a keys register still refuses that key; a room under the open register passes creation lineage in enforce mode and is in the index at creation; the configuration check reads the new file.\n\nLimits: public rooms are not deleted, so storage grows. The rate limits bound floods, but a retention policy comes before wide promotion. That policy is not part of this head.\n\nOrder: after the hosted archive advertisement item (489ad7c9). The browser start page for dap-demo is a separate request.","body":{"conditions":"One reviewed head on main with the dap-demo configuration, the open-register install option, the docs and the artroom-scope notice. Checker review of the exact head and one gate. The planner deploys and founds the register.","priority":"high","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}